{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Second plan review 2026-10-18 (BLOCK, 2 moves), both confirmed on origin/main f147e08242f and resolved by narrowing scope rather than adding behaviour:\n\n1. `--out`: the plan said it defaults to the packaged results file and proposed resolving `None` to `<corpus_root>/provider-parity/provider_parity_results.json`. In fact `provider_parity.py:585` has `default=None` and `main()` writes a file only inside `if args.out:` (`:630-632`), stdout otherwise; `recorded_results_path()` (`:118,:491`) is only ever read. The proposal would have introduced a default on-disk write where none exists, contradicting the story's zero-behaviour-change claim. Removed: `--out` is untouched, the Context sentence is corrected, and the provider-parity sub-path is gone from the fixed-layout list.\n\n2. `ticket-quality`: dropping it from `AGENTIC_SOLVERS` while `eval_specs/ticket-quality.eval.yaml` and the `eval_solver.py:406` dispatch remain would stop `solver_arm` short-circuiting for a spec that still runs. The whole ticket-quality retirement (enum member, spec, dispatch) is the LLM-leftovers epic's (winded-chunky-sheldrake, now certified). Removed from this story; Context names the ownership and the ordering reason. The old AC4 (`AGENTIC_SOLVERS` prints two members) is replaced by an AC that proves the spec union and the no-default-write behaviour, with `AGENTIC_SOLVERS` byte-identical to main.\n\nFile-impact reason for `provider_parity.py` updated to the spec union only."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792388499424506001,"uuid":"008a061c-0ede-45b7-a239-a6346ba3b3a7"}